# Content Block Schemas

Schemas are defined only on the server:

- `server/src/contentSchemas/registry.js` — site blocks keyed by `(page_name, section_name)`
- `server/src/contentSchemas/blockTypes.js` — types of page sections

The admin reads them from `GET /api/admin/schemas`. New labels go in `admin/public/locales/{hy,ru,en}/schema.json`.

## Block Definition

Fields declare:
- `key` — storage key
- `label`, `kind` (`string`|`text`|`url`|`email`|`phone`|`rich_text`|`image`|`select`|`list`), `help`
- `multilingual: true` — expands to `key_ru`, `key_en`, `key_hy`
- `required` — marks field as required in the JSON schema

The server builds a JSON Schema with `additionalProperties: false` (unknown keys are rejected).

## Validation Flow

1. Admin form validates draft locally via `validateDraft()`
2. On save, server validates `content_json` via AJV
3. Both reject unknown keys, ensuring schema safety
